Native Windows shader compilation uses the project's ignored developer cache:
Google shaderc 170316e2df47f621804bb6372e7fe00c10184105 (Apache-2.0),
2026-10-26 VS2022 build. Archive/executable hashes, origin and published unsigned
SLSA statement are pinned in third_party/ltx098-source-lock.json. This compiler
and its DLLs are not shipped in Git, APKs or model packs. The published statement
matches the archive digest; no signature verification is claimed.

Full code license texts accompany this directory in licenses/. Model weights
have independent LTXV Open Weights License 0.X terms and are not distributed.
No code from timmyy123/LLM-Hub is incorporated. No weights, learned parameters,
tokenizer, prompts, QNN runtime or QNN context binaries are embedded here.

The geometry, unpatchify and deterministic eight-step LinearQuadratic Euler
sampler independently port the pinned publisher's symmetric_patchifier.py,
vae_encode.py and schedulers/rf.py equations. The old distilled checkpoint's
unrounded inference times are preserved; no alternative scheduler is implied.

This is a research component outside the App and engine registry. It does not
provide T5/tokenization, VAE decoding or MP4 composition. Tests distinguish
untrained fixture graphs from trained DiT latent sampling; neither proves a
complete video pipeline, text conditioning, video quality or Android execution.
